  "overview": "**WPDS** is a light-first design system anchored on `rgba(250, 238, 249, 1)` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (17.5:1 contrast) and `rgba(254, 140, 108, 1)` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `System UI` (large display down to 14px body), unified by `8px` base corner radius and stepped `rgba(250, 238, 249, 1)` -> `rgba(255, 246, 241, 1)` surface layering.\n\nMaintained by **Washington Post**. Source: published token package (https://github.com/washingtonpost/wpds-ui-kit#readme), package `@washingtonpost/wpds-ui-kit`. Inventory: **91** colors, **0** typography steps, and **8** documented components (MIT license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 8 component tokens with documented paddings: `8px 12px`, `2px`, `6px 12px`, `12px 14px`, `10px 14px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `rgba(255, 246, 241, 1)` cards; separate sibling sections using `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Surface & Stroke Elevation**: Relies on crisp tonal contrast (`rgba(250, 238, 249, 1)` -> `rgba(255, 246, 241, 1)`) and `1px solid color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines instead of heavy drop shadows.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `rgba(254, 140, 108, 1)` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `rgba(250, 238, 249, 1)` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `rgba(254, 140, 108, 1)` with `#0b0b0c` text (8.6:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `System UI` headings with `System UI` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `8px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (8px on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `rgba(255, 246, 241, 1)` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `8px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input` fields and secondary buttons."
}
